      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.57,
          "end": 1.65,
          "en": "If you take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.65,
          "end": 5.07,
          "en": "at the official DatePipe documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.07,
          "end": 7.56,
          "en": "at the usage notes there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.56,
          "end": 10.83,
          "en": "you see that there are some format options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.83,
          "end": 13.62,
          "en": "that can be set for this pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.62,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "Some pre-configured templates you could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 21.36,
          "en": "where you can quickly change between some popular ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.36,
          "end": 23.193,
          "en": "of showing a date and time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.18,
          "end": 27.69,
          "en": "And then you could also configure it in great detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.69,
          "end": 29.76,
          "en": "with custom format options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.76,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "where you could control in detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 34.47,
          "en": "how the year and how the month",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.47,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "and so on should be displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 38.73,
          "en": "And you see examples",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.73,
          "end": 41.1,
          "en": "for these different options down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.1,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "in the format examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 47.37,
          "en": "This is how you could set up a complex custom output style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.37,
          "end": 49.62,
          "en": "Either way, what you can also see down here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.62,
          "end": 53.34,
          "en": "is that a pipe is configured by adding a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.34,
          "end": 55.08,
          "en": "after the pipe name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.08,
          "end": 60.06,
          "en": "that separates the pipe name from its arguments, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.06,
          "end": 63.54,
          "en": "And these configuration values are in the end arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.54,
          "end": 65.583,
          "en": "that are passed into that pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.48,
          "end": 69.57,
          "en": "So if I want to use this medium style here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.57,
          "end": 74.16,
          "en": "I could achieve this by adding a colon after date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.16,
          "end": 79.16,
          "en": "and then by passing medium as a string value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 80.64,
          "en": "to this date pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 82.083,
          "en": "So after this colon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 86.67,
          "en": "That's how we could pass this configuration value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.67,
          "end": 89.163,
          "en": "this argument into this date pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 94.11,
          "en": "And then the date pipe will format this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 96.753,
          "en": "with this configuration in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "So if you save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "and you go back, the date now looks like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 105.99000000000001,
          "en": "which is much better in my opinion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.99000000000001,
          "end": 110.99000000000001,
          "en": "So that's how you can use and configure built-in pipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.12,
          "end": 113.64,
          "en": "Now let's use this newly gained knowledge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.64,
          "end": 116.4,
          "en": "to also configure these temperatures here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.4,
          "end": 120.003,
          "en": "so that we only see a limited number of decimal points here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.02,
          "end": 125.01,
          "en": "And we can do that with help of the decimal pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.01,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "Therefore, you can, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 129.51,
          "en": "absolutely also pause the video here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.51,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "and try using that pipe on your own",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134.07,
          "en": "with help of the usage nodes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.07,
          "end": 136.29,
          "en": "so that you format these numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 138.84,
          "en": "such that we see at least one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.84,
          "end": 143.84,
          "en": "but at most two decimal places for every value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 148.14,
          "en": "After a short pause, which you can use to pause the video,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.14,
          "end": 150.243,
          "en": "we'll update this code together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.16,
          "end": 153.32999999999998,
          "en": "Did you succeed?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.32999999999998,
          "end": 155.67000000000002,
          "en": "Let's format it together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.67000000000002,
          "end": 160.47,
          "en": "For that, I of course add this pipe symbol again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.47,
          "end": 164.34,
          "en": "and then I will add the number pipe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.34,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "because even though it's called decimal pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "in the documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 170.61,
          "en": "you can learn in the usage notes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.61,
          "end": 174.18,
          "en": "that it's actually the name number that must be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.18,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "after this pipe symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 178.32,
          "en": "So number it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.32,
          "end": 180.57,
          "en": "And then we can also configure this pipe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 182.43,
          "en": "by passing a colon here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.43,
          "end": 185.73,
          "en": "And then as a string, we define the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.73,
          "end": 190.17,
          "en": "of digits in front and after the decimal separator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.17,
          "end": 192.39,
          "en": "by specifying the minimum number of digits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.39,
          "end": 194.52,
          "en": "in front of the decimal separator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.52,
          "end": 198.51,
          "en": "so one, maybe, and then the decimal separator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.51,
          "end": 202.2,
          "en": "and then the minimum and maximum amount of digits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 205.113,
          "en": "after this decimal separator, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.25,
          "end": 210.693,
          "en": "That's what you also see here in the official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 214.263,
          "en": "You also see some examples there, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.12,
          "end": 219.42000000000002,
          "en": "So with that, the number here should be formatted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.42000000000002,
          "end": 220.56,
          "en": "accordingly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.56,
          "end": 225.09,
          "en": "and therefore we can add this here to all these values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.09,
          "end": 228.39,
          "en": "But of course, like this, the pipe won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.39,
          "end": 231.15,
          "en": "Instead it needs to be unlocked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.15,
          "end": 233.4,
          "en": "Hence, we need to go to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 237.45,
          "en": "and then there add the DecimalPipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.45,
          "end": 240.273,
          "en": "imported and added to the imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.13,
          "end": 243.51,
          "en": "With that, it is unlocked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.51,
          "end": 245.46,
          "en": "And if we now save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.46,
          "end": 248.433,
          "en": "these numbers are formatted in a nicer way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.3,
          "end": 251.85,
          "en": "So that is how we can use built-in pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 251.85,
          "end": 253.8,
          "en": "and how we can configure them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 253.8,
          "end": 256.503,
          "en": "Next, I wanna build a custom pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
